<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92078" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥᾳδιουργ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>do things with ease</i> or <i>offhand</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷα πολλὰ ἡ θεὸς</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὐχή</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">
			ῥ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Herm.</u>
				71
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>act thoughtlessly</i> or <i>recklessly, do wrong, play the
				rogue</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλέπτει, τελωνεῖ, ῥᾳδιουργεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Apollod.Com.
					13.13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.602a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. ἐν ταῖς ἐφημερίσι</span>
			<i>make fraudulent entries</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				829d
			</span></i>; of writers on Alexander the Great, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				11.6.4
			</span></i>: c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστολάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>Vit.</u>
					65
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				42.16
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαθήκη ἐραδιουργημένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PVat.</u>
					11r
				</span></i>
			.<i><span class="en">
				7.41
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>live a lazy life, take things easily</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προνοεῖν, φιλοπονεῖν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.6.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.1.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.4.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Oec.</u>
				20.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hier.</u>
				8.9
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνοὺς πλεῖστα</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλείστους</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ῥᾳδιουργεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lac.</u>
					5.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> c. acc.,
				<i>treat slightingly, neglect</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἀλήθειαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					1.12
				</span></i>
			.</div>
